  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ifakara Health Institute - Empower II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Numbers of maternal and newborn deaths in Tanzania remain too high. Though child deaths have gone down in the last decade (Tanzania is on track to reach its Millennium Development Goal (MDG) target for child health), the rate of newborn deaths has hardly changed. Maternal death rates have also reduced but are nowhere near the MDG target. Given Tanzania has supportive policies on maternal, newborn and child health, why should this be? The reason lies with weak health systems. Ambitious policies and plans are held back by problems such as shortages of staff, lack of good data needed to plan health services and poor management. These problems result in poor quality health services, which put people off using them. This project (called Empower II) will refine and expand the experiences gathered in four districts during the Empower project (funded by Comic Relief) to six new districts. It is based on the belief that improving the quality of health services will increase the use of health services and lead to better health. Different combinations of activities will be tested in six districts. The project will assess the cost and cost-effectiveness of the different interventions, and inform policy makers on the best mix to improve the health of mothers, newborns and children. The project will also complete the work in the original four districts, and document how to include the interventions in district health systems, and share this learning.</narrative>
  </description>
